2. In this Order —
“casino chip” and “special employee” have the meanings given by section 2(1) of the Casino Control Act 2006;
[S 656/2026 wef 21/09/2026]
“gaming machine” has the meaning given by section 7(6) of the Gambling Control Act 2022;
“gaming machine licensee” means a person to whom a licence is granted under section 54 of the Gambling Control Act 2022 to conduct gaming involving gaming machines;
“general remote gambling” has the meaning given by section 11(1) of the Gambling Control Act 2022;
“patron” and “patron account” have the meanings given by section 139(5) of the Casino Control Act 2006.

3. The following classes of persons are exempt from section 412(1)(d) of the Act:
(a)any special employee who receives money, casino chips, or other consideration, from a patron, or from a person acting on behalf of a patron, for the purpose of depositing the money, casino chips, or other consideration, into a patron account to engage in gambling in a casino;
[S 656/2026 wef 21/09/2026]
(b)any employee of Singapore Pools (Private) Limited who receives money from a customer, or from a person acting on behalf of a customer, for the purpose of depositing the money into an account with Singapore Pools (Private) Limited to engage in general remote gambling;
(c)any employee of a gaming machine licensee who receives money from a customer, or from a person acting on behalf of a customer, as advance payment for the use of gaming machines.
